silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_01_olog_as_typed_english_sections_01_olog_definition_spivak_kent_concrete_anchor_5_R_O#pathequationdeclaration silm:hasLongDescription "The PathEquationDeclaration is the path-equation set declaring which O_eng compositions commute (e.g., has-body-mass composed with is-measured-by = total-mass-measurement-of). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'R_O', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
